1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,365
One truck company gained more than fifty-five

2
00:00:03,365 --> 00:00:05,758
thousand sales in a single year.

3
00:00:05,938 --> 00:00:09,154
Another lost almost fifty-three thousand.

4
00:00:09,334 --> 00:00:12,146
And the whole American pickup market barely

5
00:00:12,146 --> 00:00:12,538
moved.

6
00:00:12,718 --> 00:00:15,066
How can the total stay flat while

7
00:00:15,066 --> 00:00:17,699
the winners and losers change places?

8
00:00:17,879 --> 00:00:20,277
This is the real story of the

9
00:00:20,277 --> 00:00:23,336
truck brand war in twenty twenty-six.

10
00:00:23,685 --> 00:00:26,150
Every year, the pickup market looks like

11
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:27,691
a calm lake from the air.

12
00:00:27,871 --> 00:00:29,459
Millions of trucks,

13
00:00:29,459 --> 00:00:31,298
the same famous names,

14
00:00:31,298 --> 00:00:32,886
the same top three.

15
00:00:33,066 --> 00:00:35,795
But underneath, the water is moving.

16
00:00:35,975 --> 00:00:38,794
Companies gain buyers in one corner and

17
00:00:38,794 --> 00:00:40,312
lose them in another,

18
00:00:40,312 --> 00:00:42,697
and the headline numbers hide it.

19
00:00:42,877 --> 00:00:43,619
To see it,

20
00:00:43,619 --> 00:00:45,772
you have to add the trucks up

21
00:00:45,772 --> 00:00:46,886
brand by brand,

22
00:00:46,886 --> 00:00:49,484
and compare the same nine months in

23
00:00:49,484 --> 00:00:50,969
two different years.

24
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:53,247
So that is what we did.

25
00:00:53,427 --> 00:00:56,361
We took the nine-month sales table that

26
00:00:56,361 --> 00:01:00,122
Pickup Truck Talk published for twenty twenty-six,

27
00:01:00,122 --> 00:01:03,356
with the same period of twenty twenty-five,

28
00:01:03,356 --> 00:01:06,140
and added up every pickup by company.

29
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:08,750
Ford, General Motors,

30
00:01:08,750 --> 00:01:11,876
Stellantis, Toyota, Nissan,

31
00:01:11,876 --> 00:01:13,959
Honda and Hyundai.

32
00:01:14,139 --> 00:01:16,798
Please note that these totals are our

33
00:01:16,798 --> 00:01:19,097
own calculation from that table,

34
00:01:19,097 --> 00:01:21,468
and that they count the models in

35
00:01:21,468 --> 00:01:22,546
the table only,

36
00:01:22,546 --> 00:01:25,276
not the medium-duty trucks and not the

37
00:01:25,276 --> 00:01:25,923
startups.

38
00:01:26,274 --> 00:01:28,596
The result is a surprise.

39
00:01:28,776 --> 00:01:31,255
In the first nine months of twenty

40
00:01:31,255 --> 00:01:34,319
twenty-six, those trucks added up to about

41
00:01:34,319 --> 00:01:37,820
two million, three hundred twenty-four thousand.

42
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,094
In the same months of twenty twenty-five,

43
00:01:41,094 --> 00:01:42,452
about two million,

44
00:01:42,452 --> 00:01:44,792
three hundred sixteen thousand.

45
00:01:44,972 --> 00:01:47,454
That is a change of three tenths

46
00:01:47,454 --> 00:01:48,617
of one percent.

47
00:01:48,797 --> 00:01:50,434
The market is flat.

48
00:01:50,614 --> 00:01:52,952
But inside that flat number,

49
00:01:52,952 --> 00:01:56,042
one company grew by eighteen percent,

50
00:01:56,042 --> 00:01:59,298
and another one shrank by almost seven.

51
00:01:59,649 --> 00:02:00,563
Stay with me,

52
00:02:00,563 --> 00:02:02,885
because there is a twist in every

53
00:02:02,885 --> 00:02:04,362
one of these stories.

54
00:02:04,542 --> 00:02:06,649
The biggest gain came from a truck

55
00:02:06,649 --> 00:02:08,632
brand that was supposed to be in

56
00:02:08,632 --> 00:02:09,128
trouble.

57
00:02:09,308 --> 00:02:11,998
The biggest loss came from the brand

58
00:02:11,998 --> 00:02:14,463
that has led America for decades.

59
00:02:14,643 --> 00:02:17,380
One company is celebrated for a truck

60
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:19,229
that sold thirteen units.

61
00:02:19,409 --> 00:02:21,997
And one brand is quietly losing a

62
00:02:21,997 --> 00:02:23,565
third of its buyers.

63
00:02:23,745 --> 00:02:26,704
Every number comes from a published source,

64
00:02:26,704 --> 00:02:28,494
listed in the description.

65
00:02:28,844 --> 00:02:30,721
Number one is Stellantis,

66
00:02:30,721 --> 00:02:33,125
the company behind Ram and Jeep,

67
00:02:33,125 --> 00:02:35,453
and it is the biggest winner in

68
00:02:35,453 --> 00:02:36,204
the table.

69
00:02:36,384 --> 00:02:39,545
Through nine months of twenty twenty-six,

70
00:02:39,545 --> 00:02:43,555
Ram pickups sold three hundred twenty-five thousand,

71
00:02:43,555 --> 00:02:45,559
three hundred forty-eight,

72
00:02:45,559 --> 00:02:47,332
up twenty-four percent.

73
00:02:47,512 --> 00:02:50,580
The Jeep Gladiator sold thirty thousand,

74
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:52,420
nine hundred forty-four,

75
00:02:52,420 --> 00:02:54,490
down almost twenty percent.

76
00:02:54,670 --> 00:02:58,113
Put them together and Stellantis sold three

77
00:02:58,113 --> 00:03:00,275
hundred fifty-six thousand,

78
00:03:00,275 --> 00:03:02,677
two hundred ninety-two trucks,

79
00:03:02,677 --> 00:03:04,759
up about eighteen percent.

80
00:03:05,110 --> 00:03:07,712
That is an extra fifty-five thousand,

81
00:03:07,712 --> 00:03:10,876
three hundred ninety-three trucks in a single

82
00:03:10,876 --> 00:03:11,228
year.

83
00:03:11,408 --> 00:03:13,000
And in our calculation,

84
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:16,185
Stellantis went from about thirteen percent of

85
00:03:16,185 --> 00:03:18,815
these trucks to about fifteen percent.

86
00:03:18,995 --> 00:03:21,594
Two full points of the whole market,

87
00:03:21,594 --> 00:03:22,460
in one year,

88
00:03:22,460 --> 00:03:23,976
is a very large move.

89
00:03:24,156 --> 00:03:26,289
It happened in a year in which

90
00:03:26,289 --> 00:03:28,565
Ram canceled its electric truck,

91
00:03:28,565 --> 00:03:30,982
and delayed the replacement again.

92
00:03:31,162 --> 00:03:32,801
The truck that was not on sale

93
00:03:32,801 --> 00:03:34,657
did not hurt the trucks that were.

94
00:03:35,007 --> 00:03:37,276
Look inside the Ram number for the

95
00:03:37,276 --> 00:03:37,677
twist.

96
00:03:37,857 --> 00:03:39,467
The light-duty Ram,

97
00:03:39,467 --> 00:03:42,009
the one thousand five hundred,

98
00:03:42,009 --> 00:03:44,551
sold two hundred two thousand,

99
00:03:44,551 --> 00:03:46,584
one hundred forty-seven,

100
00:03:46,584 --> 00:03:48,364
up forty-one percent.

101
00:03:48,544 --> 00:03:50,616
In the third quarter alone,

102
00:03:50,616 --> 00:03:53,071
it jumped seventy-three percent,

103
00:03:53,071 --> 00:03:54,989
from forty-four thousand,

104
00:03:54,989 --> 00:03:58,749
three hundred forty-nine to seventy-six thousand,

105
00:03:58,749 --> 00:04:00,131
six hundred fifty.

106
00:04:00,311 --> 00:04:01,478
In this table,

107
00:04:01,478 --> 00:04:05,316
Ram is now the fastest-growing full-size truck

108
00:04:05,316 --> 00:04:07,068
brand in the country.

109
00:04:07,418 --> 00:04:09,384
A few things might explain it,

110
00:04:09,384 --> 00:04:11,417
and we want to be careful here,

111
00:04:11,417 --> 00:04:13,843
because the sources we checked do not

112
00:04:13,843 --> 00:04:15,219
give a single reason.

113
00:04:15,399 --> 00:04:17,202
What we can say is what the

114
00:04:17,202 --> 00:04:18,070
numbers show.

115
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:20,946
Ram grew in the light-duty trucks and

116
00:04:20,946 --> 00:04:22,769
in the heavy-duty trucks,

117
00:04:22,769 --> 00:04:24,809
up three point four percent.

118
00:04:24,989 --> 00:04:27,608
It grew while Ford and General Motors

119
00:04:27,608 --> 00:04:30,156
were adjusting their electric plans.

120
00:04:30,336 --> 00:04:32,448
And it grew without a new electric

121
00:04:32,448 --> 00:04:32,820
truck.

122
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,191
So the lesson is not that electric

123
00:04:35,191 --> 00:04:37,638
trucks hurt, but that the buyer showed

124
00:04:37,638 --> 00:04:38,991
up for the gas truck.

125
00:04:39,341 --> 00:04:40,647
Number two is Ford,

126
00:04:40,647 --> 00:04:42,711
and it is the biggest loser in

127
00:04:42,711 --> 00:04:45,118
the table, although it is still the

128
00:04:45,118 --> 00:04:47,526
biggest truck brand in the country.

129
00:04:47,706 --> 00:04:49,178
Adding the F-Series,

130
00:04:49,178 --> 00:04:52,344
the Lightning, the Ranger and the Maverick,

131
00:04:52,344 --> 00:04:56,098
Ford sold about seven hundred thirty-seven thousand

132
00:04:56,098 --> 00:04:58,086
trucks through nine months,

133
00:04:58,086 --> 00:05:00,221
down six point seven percent.

134
00:05:00,401 --> 00:05:03,209
That is a loss of fifty-two thousand,

135
00:05:03,209 --> 00:05:05,637
nine hundred forty-three trucks.

136
00:05:05,817 --> 00:05:08,641
The F-Series alone fell by forty thousand,

137
00:05:08,641 --> 00:05:09,985
eight hundred eight.

138
00:05:10,336 --> 00:05:11,659
Here is the twist.

139
00:05:11,839 --> 00:05:14,912
The Lightning, which gets all the headlines,

140
00:05:14,912 --> 00:05:16,657
explains only part of it.

141
00:05:16,837 --> 00:05:20,503
It fell from twenty-three thousand and thirty-four

142
00:05:20,503 --> 00:05:21,749
to four thousand,

143
00:05:21,749 --> 00:05:23,362
seven hundred seventy,

144
00:05:23,362 --> 00:05:25,414
a drop of eighteen thousand,

145
00:05:25,414 --> 00:05:27,100
two hundred sixty-four.

146
00:05:27,280 --> 00:05:29,478
The rest of the fall came from

147
00:05:29,478 --> 00:05:31,530
the regular F-Series trucks.

148
00:05:31,710 --> 00:05:34,849
The F-Series, not counting the Lightning,

149
00:05:34,849 --> 00:05:38,295
went from five hundred ninety-seven thousand,

150
00:05:38,295 --> 00:05:41,970
five hundred forty-six to five hundred fifty-six

151
00:05:41,970 --> 00:05:44,803
thousand, seven hundred thirty-eight,

152
00:05:44,803 --> 00:05:47,023
down six point eight percent.

153
00:05:47,374 --> 00:05:48,712
In our calculation,

154
00:05:48,712 --> 00:05:51,741
Ford went from about thirty-four percent of

155
00:05:51,741 --> 00:05:54,630
these trucks to about thirty-two percent.

156
00:05:54,810 --> 00:05:56,161
Still a giant,

157
00:05:56,161 --> 00:05:57,898
but a smaller one.

158
00:05:58,078 --> 00:06:00,307
And there is a quiet bright spot.

159
00:06:00,487 --> 00:06:03,815
The Ranger rose six point nine percent,

160
00:06:03,815 --> 00:06:05,692
to fifty-one thousand,

161
00:06:05,692 --> 00:06:07,313
six hundred thirty,

162
00:06:07,313 --> 00:06:10,470
and the Maverick rose two point three

163
00:06:10,470 --> 00:06:14,395
percent, to one hundred twenty-three thousand,

164
00:06:14,395 --> 00:06:16,358
six hundred eighty-one.

165
00:06:16,538 --> 00:06:18,289
The small trucks helped,

166
00:06:18,289 --> 00:06:20,114
and the big ones did not.

167
00:06:20,464 --> 00:06:22,170
Ford's chief executive,

168
00:06:22,170 --> 00:06:24,988
Jim Farley, said in December that Ford

169
00:06:24,988 --> 00:06:27,881
would rather not spend billions more on

170
00:06:27,881 --> 00:06:30,922
large electric vehicles that have no path

171
00:06:30,922 --> 00:06:34,185
to profitability, and that hybrids have been

172
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:37,449
more popular than the company ever expected.

173
00:06:37,629 --> 00:06:40,475
Ford took a nineteen point five billion

174
00:06:40,475 --> 00:06:42,737
dollar charge to change course.

175
00:06:42,917 --> 00:06:46,083
The sales table shows what changing course

176
00:06:46,083 --> 00:06:48,270
looks like in the short term.

177
00:06:48,450 --> 00:06:50,425
When you stop making a truck,

178
00:06:50,425 --> 00:06:51,651
its sales go away,

179
00:06:51,651 --> 00:06:53,763
and the company has to win them

180
00:06:53,763 --> 00:06:55,125
back somewhere else.

181
00:06:55,476 --> 00:06:57,655
Number three is General Motors,

182
00:06:57,655 --> 00:06:59,976
the brand with the largest total,

183
00:06:59,976 --> 00:07:01,733
and a very small decline.

184
00:07:01,913 --> 00:07:03,626
Adding the Silverado,

185
00:07:03,626 --> 00:07:05,664
the Sierra, the Colorado,

186
00:07:05,664 --> 00:07:09,089
the Canyon, and the electric Silverado EV,

187
00:07:09,089 --> 00:07:11,046
Sierra EV and Hummer EV,

188
00:07:11,046 --> 00:07:15,041
GM sold about seven hundred eighty-seven thousand

189
00:07:15,041 --> 00:07:17,242
trucks through nine months,

190
00:07:17,242 --> 00:07:19,607
down one point eight percent.

191
00:07:19,787 --> 00:07:21,282
In our calculation,

192
00:07:21,282 --> 00:07:23,879
GM is now slightly ahead of Ford,

193
00:07:23,879 --> 00:07:27,421
with about thirty-four percent of the trucks,

194
00:07:27,421 --> 00:07:30,097
against about thirty-two for Ford.

195
00:07:30,447 --> 00:07:32,810
Look at what is inside that number,

196
00:07:32,810 --> 00:07:34,566
because it is a story of a

197
00:07:34,566 --> 00:07:37,402
company holding steady with one hand while

198
00:07:37,402 --> 00:07:38,887
losing with the other.

199
00:07:39,067 --> 00:07:40,925
The gas trucks did fine.

200
00:07:41,105 --> 00:07:43,726
The Silverado was down less than one

201
00:07:43,726 --> 00:07:44,309
percent.

202
00:07:44,489 --> 00:07:47,282
The Sierra was up three tenths of

203
00:07:47,282 --> 00:07:48,297
one percent.

204
00:07:48,477 --> 00:07:50,857
The Canyon was up twenty percent.

205
00:07:51,037 --> 00:07:53,136
But the three electric lines,

206
00:07:53,136 --> 00:07:54,366
the Silverado EV,

207
00:07:54,366 --> 00:07:56,683
the Sierra EV and the Hummer EV,

208
00:07:56,683 --> 00:08:00,012
fell from about twenty-eight thousand to about

209
00:08:00,012 --> 00:08:01,242
fifteen thousand.

210
00:08:01,593 --> 00:08:03,079
That is the twist.

211
00:08:03,259 --> 00:08:05,864
General Motors lost less than most of

212
00:08:05,864 --> 00:08:08,189
its rivals, and the reason is the

213
00:08:08,189 --> 00:08:10,794
gas trucks carrying the weight of the

214
00:08:10,794 --> 00:08:11,780
electric ones.

215
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:15,365
The heavy-duty Silverado fell thirteen percent,

216
00:08:15,365 --> 00:08:18,118
from one hundred fifty-three thousand,

217
00:08:18,118 --> 00:08:21,523
seven hundred fifty to one hundred thirty-three

218
00:08:21,523 --> 00:08:24,058
thousand, seven hundred sixty-nine.

219
00:08:24,238 --> 00:08:27,323
But the light-duty Silverado grew six point

220
00:08:27,323 --> 00:08:28,255
five percent.

221
00:08:28,435 --> 00:08:29,716
In a flat market,

222
00:08:29,716 --> 00:08:32,129
a company with a wide lineup can

223
00:08:32,129 --> 00:08:33,485
hide a bad corner.

224
00:08:33,836 --> 00:08:35,673
Number four is Toyota,

225
00:08:35,673 --> 00:08:38,178
and its story is the quietest.

226
00:08:38,358 --> 00:08:41,046
Adding the Tundra and the Tacoma,

227
00:08:41,046 --> 00:08:44,874
Toyota sold three hundred twenty-four thousand,

228
00:08:44,874 --> 00:08:47,399
nine hundred fifty-five trucks,

229
00:08:47,399 --> 00:08:48,783
up three percent.

230
00:08:48,963 --> 00:08:50,310
In our calculation,

231
00:08:50,310 --> 00:08:53,144
its share rose from about thirteen point

232
00:08:53,144 --> 00:08:55,837
six percent to about fourteen percent.

233
00:08:56,017 --> 00:08:57,410
Nothing dramatic.

234
00:08:57,590 --> 00:08:59,035
But in a flat market,

235
00:08:59,035 --> 00:09:01,444
a company that gains a little every

236
00:09:01,444 --> 00:09:03,715
year is gaining at the expense of

237
00:09:03,715 --> 00:09:04,266
someone.

238
00:09:04,616 --> 00:09:07,611
And here is the twist inside Toyota.

239
00:09:07,791 --> 00:09:10,132
All of the growth came from the

240
00:09:10,132 --> 00:09:12,699
Tacoma, up five point one percent,

241
00:09:12,699 --> 00:09:15,191
to two hundred fourteen thousand,

242
00:09:15,191 --> 00:09:17,230
eight hundred seventy-five.

243
00:09:17,410 --> 00:09:20,081
The Tundra, the full-size truck,

244
00:09:20,081 --> 00:09:23,002
was down eight tenths of a percent,

245
00:09:23,002 --> 00:09:26,257
to one hundred ten thousand and eighty.

246
00:09:26,437 --> 00:09:28,737
Toyota is winning in the middle of

247
00:09:28,737 --> 00:09:30,969
the market and holding in the big

248
00:09:30,969 --> 00:09:33,270
one, and the company does not have

249
00:09:33,270 --> 00:09:35,434
to invent anything new to do it.

250
00:09:35,785 --> 00:09:37,376
Number five is Nissan,

251
00:09:37,376 --> 00:09:39,836
and it is the strangest company on

252
00:09:39,836 --> 00:09:40,487
the list.

253
00:09:40,667 --> 00:09:43,407
Adding the Titan and the Frontier,

254
00:09:43,407 --> 00:09:45,906
Nissan sold sixty-six thousand,

255
00:09:45,906 --> 00:09:50,016
five hundred twenty-six trucks through nine months,

256
00:09:50,016 --> 00:09:51,870
up thirty-four percent.

257
00:09:52,050 --> 00:09:54,539
That is the highest growth rate of

258
00:09:54,539 --> 00:09:56,369
any company in the table.

259
00:09:56,549 --> 00:09:58,475
And it happened in a year in

260
00:09:58,475 --> 00:10:01,019
which the Titan sold thirteen trucks.

261
00:10:01,369 --> 00:10:02,924
Yes, thirteen.

262
00:10:03,104 --> 00:10:04,229
A year earlier,

263
00:10:04,229 --> 00:10:07,528
the Titan sold two thousand and twenty-four.

264
00:10:07,708 --> 00:10:10,761
Nissan ended the full-size truck after the

265
00:10:10,761 --> 00:10:12,941
twenty twenty-four model year,

266
00:10:12,941 --> 00:10:14,977
as Motor Authority reported,

267
00:10:14,977 --> 00:10:17,303
and the numbers are now just the

268
00:10:17,303 --> 00:10:19,411
last trucks leaving the lots.

269
00:10:19,591 --> 00:10:21,718
But the Frontier more than made up

270
00:10:21,718 --> 00:10:22,156
for it.

271
00:10:22,336 --> 00:10:24,994
It rose from forty-seven thousand,

272
00:10:24,994 --> 00:10:28,198
six hundred thirty to sixty-six thousand,

273
00:10:28,198 --> 00:10:29,918
five hundred thirteen.

274
00:10:30,098 --> 00:10:32,262
A company can grow by ending a

275
00:10:32,262 --> 00:10:34,498
truck, if the truck it keeps is

276
00:10:34,498 --> 00:10:35,508
the right one.

277
00:10:35,858 --> 00:10:38,063
Number six is the pair at the

278
00:10:38,063 --> 00:10:39,584
bottom of the table,

279
00:10:39,584 --> 00:10:40,953
Honda and Hyundai,

280
00:10:40,953 --> 00:10:43,311
and they tell opposite stories.

281
00:10:43,491 --> 00:10:47,046
The Honda Ridgeline sold thirty-seven thousand and

282
00:10:47,046 --> 00:10:49,392
twenty-eight through nine months,

