00:12:17,950 --> 00:12:20,737
The Maverick grew twenty point four percent.

326
00:12:20,917 --> 00:12:23,157
The Canyon grew almost eighteen.

327
00:12:23,337 --> 00:12:26,395
But the Toyota Tacoma slipped three and

328
00:12:26,395 --> 00:12:27,572
a half percent,

329
00:12:27,572 --> 00:12:30,394
the GMC Sierra slipped six tenths of

330
00:12:30,394 --> 00:12:33,374
a percent, and the Gladiator fell more

331
00:12:33,374 --> 00:12:34,158
than nine.

332
00:12:34,508 --> 00:12:35,708
The Ram trucks,

333
00:12:35,708 --> 00:12:39,627
meanwhile, rose almost thirty-four percent in the

334
00:12:39,627 --> 00:12:43,787
quarter, from eighty-eight thousand and sixty-six to

335
00:12:43,787 --> 00:12:46,267
one hundred seventeen thousand,

336
00:12:46,267 --> 00:12:48,347
seven hundred fifty-seven.

337
00:12:48,527 --> 00:12:51,678
The Nissan Frontier rose thirty-seven and a

338
00:12:51,678 --> 00:12:52,045
half.

339
00:12:52,225 --> 00:12:55,316
And the Santa Cruz fell almost twenty-five

340
00:12:55,316 --> 00:12:55,905
percent.

341
00:12:56,085 --> 00:12:58,462
So the winners stayed the winners,

342
00:12:58,462 --> 00:13:00,839
and the biggest loser of the year,

343
00:13:00,839 --> 00:13:02,586
Ford, started to recover.

344
00:13:02,766 --> 00:13:05,684
A nine-month table tells you the direction,

345
00:13:05,684 --> 00:13:08,262
and the latest quarter tells you where

346
00:13:08,262 --> 00:13:09,280
the road bends.

347
00:13:09,630 --> 00:13:11,954
This is why we always read two

348
00:13:11,954 --> 00:13:13,890
windows at the same time.

349
00:13:14,070 --> 00:13:16,364
If you only read the nine months,

350
00:13:16,364 --> 00:13:18,657
you might believe Ford is in free

351
00:13:18,657 --> 00:13:19,005
fall.

352
00:13:19,185 --> 00:13:21,238
If you only read the third quarter,

353
00:13:21,238 --> 00:13:23,701
you might believe nothing happened at all.

354
00:13:23,881 --> 00:13:25,059
Both are true,

355
00:13:25,059 --> 00:13:27,585
and neither is the full story.

356
00:13:27,765 --> 00:13:29,747
A company can be losing for the

357
00:13:29,747 --> 00:13:31,857
year and recovering at the end of

358
00:13:31,857 --> 00:13:32,049
it.

359
00:13:32,229 --> 00:13:34,428
And a buyer who understands that can

360
00:13:34,428 --> 00:13:36,873
ask a better question at the dealership.

361
00:13:37,223 --> 00:13:39,208
What does that mean at the dealership?

362
00:13:39,388 --> 00:13:41,407
It means that a brand that lost

363
00:13:41,407 --> 00:13:43,816
ground and is now recovering might be

364
00:13:43,816 --> 00:13:46,486
willing to negotiate to keep the recovery

365
00:13:46,486 --> 00:13:46,876
going.

366
00:13:47,056 --> 00:13:49,173
And a brand that is growing quickly

367
00:13:49,173 --> 00:13:51,410
might have fewer reasons to discount.

368
00:13:51,590 --> 00:13:53,680
We cannot promise which one you will

369
00:13:53,680 --> 00:13:53,970
find.

370
00:13:54,150 --> 00:13:56,380
But we can tell you that Cox

371
00:13:56,380 --> 00:14:00,202
Automotive measured incentives at six point five

372
00:14:00,202 --> 00:14:03,308
percent of the average price in August,

373
00:14:03,308 --> 00:14:06,095
down from seven point two percent a

374
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:07,130
year earlier.

375
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:09,500
A final point about what a table

376
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:11,648
like this can and cannot tell you.

377
00:14:11,828 --> 00:14:14,401
It counts trucks sold in the United

378
00:14:14,401 --> 00:14:15,798
States, by company.

379
00:14:15,978 --> 00:14:18,384
It does not count the quality of

380
00:14:18,384 --> 00:14:20,941
the truck, or how happy the owners

381
00:14:20,941 --> 00:14:23,196
are, or how much each one cost

382
00:14:23,196 --> 00:14:23,873
to build.

383
00:14:24,053 --> 00:14:26,463
A truck can sell well because it

384
00:14:26,463 --> 00:14:28,646
is good, because it is cheap,

385
00:14:28,646 --> 00:14:31,206
because the company discounted it,

386
00:14:31,206 --> 00:14:34,067
or because a fleet bought thousands at

387
00:14:34,067 --> 00:14:34,444
once.

388
00:14:34,624 --> 00:14:37,283
Sales tell you what buyers did.

389
00:14:37,463 --> 00:14:39,111
They do not tell you why.

390
00:14:39,462 --> 00:14:41,210
That is why we pair every sales

391
00:14:41,210 --> 00:14:42,902
number with a check you can do

392
00:14:42,902 --> 00:14:43,409
yourself.

393
00:14:43,589 --> 00:14:46,676
Look up the reliability record of the

394
00:14:46,676 --> 00:14:48,094
exact model year.

395
00:14:48,274 --> 00:14:49,899
Read the owner reviews.

396
00:14:50,079 --> 00:14:52,496
Compare the price of the same trim

397
00:14:52,496 --> 00:14:53,562
at two dealers.

398
00:14:53,742 --> 00:14:54,915
And look at the warranty.

399
00:14:55,095 --> 00:14:57,410
A sales number can tell you which

400
00:14:57,410 --> 00:14:58,603
truck is popular,

401
00:14:58,603 --> 00:15:01,059
but only you can decide which truck

402
00:15:01,059 --> 00:15:03,024
is right for the work you do

403
00:15:03,024 --> 00:15:04,638
and the money you have.

404
00:15:04,988 --> 00:15:07,285
So let's put the whole race in

405
00:15:07,285 --> 00:15:08,204
one picture.

406
00:15:08,384 --> 00:15:11,449
Stellantis gained about two points of share.

407
00:15:11,629 --> 00:15:14,546
Nissan gained about eight tenths of a

408
00:15:14,546 --> 00:15:15,019
point.

409
00:15:15,199 --> 00:15:17,498
Toyota gained about four tenths.

410
00:15:17,678 --> 00:15:19,129
Honda stayed the same.

411
00:15:19,309 --> 00:15:21,573
Hyundai lost three tenths.

412
00:15:21,753 --> 00:15:24,783
General Motors lost seven tenths.

413
00:15:24,963 --> 00:15:27,321
And Ford lost two and a half

414
00:15:27,321 --> 00:15:30,520
points, the biggest loss in the table,

415
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:32,962
almost two and a half points.

416
00:15:33,142 --> 00:15:36,602
These are our calculations from published sales,

417
00:15:36,602 --> 00:15:39,196
rounded, and they show who is taking

418
00:15:39,196 --> 00:15:40,422
buyers from whom.

419
00:15:40,772 --> 00:15:43,012
Now here is the final twist.

420
00:15:43,192 --> 00:15:45,791
Total trucks in the table grew by

421
00:15:45,791 --> 00:15:48,626
about eight thousand in nine months.

422
00:15:48,806 --> 00:15:51,683
But Stellantis alone grew by more than

423
00:15:51,683 --> 00:15:55,091
fifty-five thousand, and Ford alone shrank by

424
00:15:55,091 --> 00:15:57,211
almost fifty-three thousand.

425
00:15:57,391 --> 00:15:59,116
So the market did not grow,

426
00:15:59,116 --> 00:16:01,414
and the winners took the trucks from

427
00:16:01,414 --> 00:16:02,117
the losers.

428
00:16:02,297 --> 00:16:04,790
In a market this big and this

429
00:16:04,790 --> 00:16:07,370
stable, a buyer is rarely new.

430
00:16:07,550 --> 00:16:10,653
A buyer is almost always a buyer

431
00:16:10,653 --> 00:16:13,077
taken from somebody else.

432
00:16:13,427 --> 00:16:15,029
Why does that matter to you?

433
00:16:15,209 --> 00:16:17,653
Because the brand that is gaining has

434
00:16:17,653 --> 00:16:19,238
a reason to make a deal,

435
00:16:19,238 --> 00:16:21,352
and the brand that is losing has

436
00:16:21,352 --> 00:16:23,201
a reason to make a deal too,

437
00:16:23,201 --> 00:16:24,984
just for different reasons.

438
00:16:25,164 --> 00:16:27,480
And the truck you cross-shop is probably

439
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:29,332
the one that went the other way.

440
00:16:29,512 --> 00:16:31,322
If you are looking at a Ford,

441
00:16:31,322 --> 00:16:33,007
check what Ram is offering.

442
00:16:33,187 --> 00:16:34,994
If you are looking at a Ram,

443
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:37,447
check what Ford and General Motors are

444
00:16:37,447 --> 00:16:38,028
offering.

445
00:16:38,208 --> 00:16:41,042
Competition is the most useful tool a

446
00:16:41,042 --> 00:16:41,807
buyer has.

447
00:16:42,158 --> 00:16:45,161
Let's turn the share numbers into something

448
00:16:45,161 --> 00:16:46,279
a buyer can use.

449
00:16:46,459 --> 00:16:49,910
Remember that in our calculation Stellantis moved

450
00:16:49,910 --> 00:16:52,938
from about thirteen percent of these trucks

451
00:16:52,938 --> 00:16:54,698
to about fifteen percent,

452
00:16:54,698 --> 00:16:57,515
and Ford from about thirty-four to about

453
00:16:57,515 --> 00:16:58,290
thirty-two.

454
00:16:58,470 --> 00:17:00,754
A shift like that does not mean

455
00:17:00,754 --> 00:17:03,039
one truck is good and the other

456
00:17:03,039 --> 00:17:03,555
is bad.

457
00:17:03,735 --> 00:17:06,334
It means more buyers chose one badge

458
00:17:06,334 --> 00:17:07,055
this year.

459
00:17:07,235 --> 00:17:09,050
Treat it as a clue about where

460
00:17:09,050 --> 00:17:10,078
dealers are busy,

461
00:17:10,078 --> 00:17:12,013
and where they may be hungry for

462
00:17:12,013 --> 00:17:12,437
a sale.

463
00:17:12,787 --> 00:17:14,792
Before you buy any truck,

464
00:17:14,792 --> 00:17:15,754
new or used,

465
00:17:15,754 --> 00:17:19,684
run the vehicle identification number through the

466
00:17:19,684 --> 00:17:21,529
official recall lookup.

467
00:17:21,709 --> 00:17:22,459
It is free,

468
00:17:22,459 --> 00:17:23,685
it takes a minute,

469
00:17:23,685 --> 00:17:25,934
and it tells you whether a safety

470
00:17:25,934 --> 00:17:28,115
fix is still open for that exact

471
00:17:28,115 --> 00:17:28,524
truck.

472
00:17:28,704 --> 00:17:31,339
This matters more with a truck from

473
00:17:31,339 --> 00:17:33,748
a brand in the middle of change,

474
00:17:33,748 --> 00:17:36,158
because lineups and plans shift.

475
00:17:36,338 --> 00:17:38,479
Do the same for the model year

476
00:17:38,479 --> 00:17:41,049
you want, and read what other owners

477
00:17:41,049 --> 00:17:43,120
say about that specific year,

478
00:17:43,120 --> 00:17:44,476
not only the badge.

479
00:17:44,826 --> 00:17:45,812
Now the money.

480
00:17:45,992 --> 00:17:48,907
Ask every dealer for the out-the-door price

481
00:17:48,907 --> 00:17:51,415
in writing, with all fees and options

482
00:17:51,415 --> 00:17:53,855
included, and get the quotes for the

483
00:17:53,855 --> 00:17:55,617
same trim on the same day.

484
00:17:55,797 --> 00:17:58,248
A monthly payment can hide a lot,

485
00:17:58,248 --> 00:18:00,328
and a longer loan can make a

486
00:18:00,328 --> 00:18:01,962
high price feel small.

487
00:18:02,142 --> 00:18:06,001
Remember the incentives figure we gave you,

488
00:18:06,001 --> 00:18:09,321
six point five percent of the average

489
00:18:09,321 --> 00:18:10,757
price in August.

490
00:18:10,937 --> 00:18:13,417
If the discount on your quote is

491
00:18:13,417 --> 00:18:15,045
far smaller, ask why,

492
00:18:15,045 --> 00:18:16,363
and ask politely,

493
00:18:16,363 --> 00:18:18,379
and be ready to walk away.

494
00:18:18,729 --> 00:18:22,188
Last, think about who each brand suits.

495
00:18:22,368 --> 00:18:24,790
If you want the truck that many

496
00:18:24,790 --> 00:18:26,431
people already chose,

497
00:18:26,431 --> 00:18:29,712
Ford, General Motors and Toyota have large

498
00:18:29,712 --> 00:18:33,072
bases, which usually helps with service and

499
00:18:33,072 --> 00:18:33,618
resale.

500
00:18:33,798 --> 00:18:35,721
If you want a gas truck from

501
00:18:35,721 --> 00:18:37,369
a brand that is growing,

502
00:18:37,369 --> 00:18:39,360
Ram is the story of the year.

503
00:18:39,540 --> 00:18:41,424
And if you are looking at a

504
00:18:41,424 --> 00:18:43,588
truck with an uncertain future,

505
00:18:43,588 --> 00:18:44,984
like the Santa Cruz,

506
00:18:44,984 --> 00:18:46,659
wait for a clear answer,

507
00:18:46,659 --> 00:18:48,962
and ask for the warranty terms in

508
00:18:48,962 --> 00:18:51,266
writing before you sign anything.

509
00:18:51,616 --> 00:18:54,482
One more mistake is to shop only

510
00:18:54,482 --> 00:18:56,004
inside one brand.

511
00:18:56,184 --> 00:18:58,954
A buyer who walks into a single

512
00:18:58,954 --> 00:19:01,188
showroom hears one story.

513
00:19:01,368 --> 00:19:03,045
Visit at least two brands,

514
00:19:03,045 --> 00:19:05,237
and bring the quote from the first

515
00:19:05,237 --> 00:19:06,140
to the second.

516
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:09,373
Remember that Ford lost fifty-two thousand,

517
00:19:09,373 --> 00:19:13,279
nine hundred forty-three trucks while Stellantis gained

518
00:19:13,279 --> 00:19:16,687
fifty-five thousand, three hundred ninety-three.

519
00:19:16,867 --> 00:19:18,747
Those buyers did compare,

520
00:19:18,747 --> 00:19:19,874
and they moved.

521
00:19:20,054 --> 00:19:21,776
You can use the same freedom,

522
00:19:21,776 --> 00:19:23,201
and the dealer knows it.

523
00:19:23,551 --> 00:19:25,536
So what should you check before you

524
00:19:25,536 --> 00:19:27,068
buy in twenty twenty-seven?

525
00:19:27,248 --> 00:19:29,767
First, look at the sales trend of

526
00:19:29,767 --> 00:19:30,988
the exact model,

527
00:19:30,988 --> 00:19:32,438
not only the brand.

528
00:19:32,618 --> 00:19:34,932
A brand can be growing while one

529
00:19:34,932 --> 00:19:36,740
of its trucks is falling.

530
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:39,437
Second, find out whether the truck is

531
00:19:39,437 --> 00:19:40,662
still being built,

532
00:19:40,662 --> 00:19:41,819
and for how long.

533
00:19:41,999 --> 00:19:44,152
Third, compare the full cost,

534
00:19:44,152 --> 00:19:45,265
with the price,

535
00:19:45,265 --> 00:19:47,937
the financing, and the resale value,

536
00:19:47,937 --> 00:19:50,461
because a truck that sells well is

537
00:19:50,461 --> 00:19:52,761
generally easier to sell later.

538
00:19:53,112 --> 00:19:55,817
Fourth, ask for the incentives.

539
00:19:55,997 --> 00:19:59,278
The Cox Automotive report for August showed

540
00:19:59,278 --> 00:20:02,254
incentives at six point five percent of

541
00:20:02,254 --> 00:20:03,627
the average price,

542
00:20:03,627 --> 00:20:06,298
down from seven point two percent a

543
00:20:06,298 --> 00:20:08,739
year earlier, so you may have to

544
00:20:08,739 --> 00:20:09,731
ask for them.

545
00:20:09,911 --> 00:20:12,866
And fifth, remember that a flat market

546
00:20:12,866 --> 00:20:15,043
means every sale is a fight.

547
00:20:15,223 --> 00:20:16,906
You are not the one who needs

548
00:20:16,906 --> 00:20:17,835
to be convinced.

549
00:20:18,015 --> 00:20:19,153
The brand is.

550
00:20:19,503 --> 00:20:21,259
We put all of this into a

551
00:20:21,259 --> 00:20:25,122
checklist, the Twenty Twenty-Seven Truck Buyer's Guide.

552
00:20:25,302 --> 00:20:27,571
It covers the numbers to check,

553
00:20:27,571 --> 00:20:29,767
the questions to ask a dealer,

554
00:20:29,767 --> 00:20:32,402
and the warning signs we just walked

555
00:20:32,402 --> 00:20:32,988
through.

